# tests/database/staff-activation-link.test.ts — the password a test types
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Seven hits, two distinct strings, both invented for that file: they are what
# the test passes to `activateAccount` as the password a newly invited librarian
# chooses. They authenticate nothing. No account in development, in the test
# database or in production has ever had either of them, they appear in no
# environment file, and they exist only inside a suite that runs against a
# throwaway database it truncates on every test.
#
# They trip `generic-api-key` on entropy alone — four hyphenated words and a
# number is exactly the shape of a generated key, which is also why they were
# chosen: a password the real policy would accept. The alternative, weakening
# the passwords until the scanner stops noticing, would make the test prove
# less.
#
